  "instructor": [
    {
      "text": "Welcome to the capstone. Every drone you have built across the lab series — its propulsion, its mass, its power system — comes together here into one mission model: how much power it burns, how much energy it needs, and how far it can fly.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Start in Input Parameters — pick your components (the battery matters most for this capstone), then set the density altitude and payload sliders. Watch the Diagnostics Log for any build errors before you run.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Module 1 · Power Profiling sweeps airspeed from 2 to 20 m/s and plots cruise power against speed. Watch the U-shape emerge — parasitic drag rising with speed against the induced-power floor falling with it.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Module 1 · Endurance Speed reads the exact bottom of that U-curve. The speed at minimum power is the maximum-endurance speed — the airspeed that keeps the craft aloft longest per Watt-hour.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Module 2 · Mission Energy — set the takeoff, cruise, hover-on-station, return and landing durations, and watch the Watt-hour budget accumulate phase by phase. The verdict confirms whether the pack holds enough charge for the full mission.",
      "audio": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Module 2 · Range–Payload sweeps payload across three battery packs to map the range-payload envelope — the primary deliverable of any UAV mission brief. Complete it to unlock the capstone reward.",
      "audio": null
    }
  ],
